nt Tuesday it said her headscarf  fell off after she had to take part in  an event unexpectedly she said she was  flying home recabee's Instagram feed  shows multiple pictures of her covering  her hair but rarely in a full hijab  human rights campaigners think her  actions were no accident what I I  personally think is that she definitely  tried to to show her solidarity with her  Sisters in Iran climbing World governing  body says it supports athletes right to  freedom of Express oppression other  women have been banned from sport in  Iran for not dressing according to  regime rules like soccer player Shiva  amini that punishment will come  definitely if this courage goes away and  most importantly what will happen is  that her professional career will be at  risk the Iranian Embassy in Korea says  it denies all false news about rekhabi's  situation without referring to any  reports in particular the Islamic  Republic has an obligation to protect  children's right to life under any  circumstances on Tuesday the United  Nations said as many as 23 children are  among those who have died in the  Crackdown on anti-regime protests over  the past month a movement sparked by the  death of Masa amini in custody Redmond  Shannon Global News London  enduring summer in October ahead when  will British Columbia's unprecedented  dry spell relent  when most people think about the British  Columbia Coast one of the first things  that comes to mind is rain and lots of  it but this year has been much different  it's now been more than 100 days since  any significant rain fell and as Aaron  McArthur reports between the Wildfire  smoke and ultra low water levels  conditions look more like mid-august  than mid-october  22 000 people on BC's Sunshine Coast  have been living with severe water  restrictions for more than a month under  stage 4 restrictions residents and  Farmers have been banned from using  treated water for all outdoor uses  with almost no rain since the beginning  of July the regional district has been  forced to close the Taps further a local  state of emergency has been declared now  non-essential heavy commercial users of  water will be cut off the intent is  really to focus on make sure that we  have enough water for residents  philosophical for firefighting the  district's pools will be closed  breweries cideries and distilleries are  named in the order along with bottled  water companies and concrete cement and  asphalt operations  businesses affected by the order will be  compelled to stop using treated water  for Persephone Brewing the Water Crisis  has immediate impacts there's enough  stock on hand to last three weeks it's  not just about our bottom lines it's  about trying to keep our people employed  and trying to you know contribute to our  economy on the coast since July 10th the  District of sea Shelt has recorded just  nine millimeters of rain  the average for this period is 200  millimeters  BC has smashed temperature records for  October and smoke from forest fires is  still creating air quality issues  Farmers have taken Extreme Measures by  trying to conserve water  grounded Acres Farm installing storage  for roughly 34 000 liters of water  it was gone in two weeks  without enough water to plant winter  cover crops the situation could still  get worse the viability of the business  is at stake yeah I'm looking at my bare  fields and I'm looking at a lot of rain  coming down and I will lose my topsoil  while there is rain in the forecast it  isn't nearly enough to recharge the  reservoir the level needs to come up  four meters before restrictions can be  removed  Aaron McArthur Global News seashell BC  sharing her fortune next the  multi-billionaire leading the way in  giving it away  [Music]  it is being billed as the Girl Scouts of  America's biggest donation from a single  donor since its founding in 1912. more  than 80 million US Dollars earmarked for  the organization from billionaire  philanthropist Mackenzie Scott as Ross  Lord reports the historic contribution  is just the latest in a long line of  charitable gifts from the former first  lady of Amazon  like most billionaires Mackenzie Scott  would seem to have far more money than  she'll ever truly need but Scott is  doing something many billionaires don't  generously sharing her wealth in a big  way her latest charitable Endeavor is  the largest single gift in the U.S Girl  Scouts history for Scott it follows  donations to hundreds of organizations  ranging alphabetically from groups that  offer free legal advice to ones that  invest in the potential of young people  and many many others in between  465 non-profits converting 3.9 billion  dollars in gifts into services for  others overall donations are more than  twice that amount from a woman who was  once best known as the wife of Amazon  founder Jeff Bezos Scott has rarely  given interviews but while they were  still married she discussed Bezos with  talk show host Charlie Rose he offered  me a job but I interviewed with some  other people and I was offered a job at  another department too so I ended up  taking a different job but then as luck  would have it got assigned an office  right next door to his she divorced  Bezos in 2019 her stake in Amazon is  currently worth an estimated 33 billion  dollars U.S but Scott has plenty of  independent accomplishments she's a  Princeton grad a mother of four an  award-winning novelist you have wanted  to be  writer  [Music]  wrote my first book when I was six but  her gift for giving is defining her  Legacy as a rule she lets her actions  speak for her staying out of the  spotlight encouraging those interested  in her philanthropy to seek out the  organization's she invests in helping  any of us can help us all she wrote in a  public post earlier this year  Scott has promised to give away roughly  half of her Fortune which means billions  more in donations are still to come  Ross Lord Global News  and that is global n